{
  "_note": "Canonical redaction vectors for optional request logging. Shared byte for byte by sp-laravel-api-js (test/vectors/log-redaction.json) and sp-laravel-api-dart (test/vectors/log_redaction.json). The placeholder is the text <redacted>; the truncation limit is 2048 UTF-16 code units, and a longer body keeps its first 2048 and appends the marker …[truncated]. headers: input.headers is a map of header name to value and input.tenantHeader is the configured tenant header name or null; expected is the map after redaction (names keep the case they were given; sensitive names are matched case-insensitively). bodies: input is any JSON value; a JSON string is a body that was sent as text: a string holding a JSON object or array is parsed, redacted and re-serialised compactly with no spaces and keys in the original order, and a url-encoded string has its sensitive values replaced; any other string is only truncated. Sensitive keys match case-insensitively with - and _ ignored (password, access_token, refresh_token, token, code, otp, secret, api_key) or end in _token (with - read as _); a sensitive key has its whole value replaced, at any depth and inside arrays. urls: input is a full URL; query values of sensitive keys (also inside brackets) become the placeholder, credentials in the authority become the placeholder, and paths and fragments are kept.",
